{"files_reviewed":["apps/kaipu-record/src/shared/types/workspaces.ts","apps/kaipu-record/src/main/workspaces/index.ts","apps/kaipu-record/src/main/workspaces/registry.ts","apps/kaipu-record/src/main/workspaces/relocate.ts","apps/kaipu-record/src/renderer/src/features/workspaces/workspaces-context.tsx","apps/kaipu-record/src/main/workspaces/registry-relocate.test.ts","apps/kaipu-record/src/main/workspaces/relocate.test.ts"],"files_skipped":[],"findings":[{"path":"apps/kaipu-record/src/main/workspaces/registry.ts","line":718,"severity":"fix","topic":"bug","confidence":"high","title":"An offline rename of a never-initialized workspace is silently replaced when its folder returns with another identity","body":"The edit at registry.ts:634 now keeps `pendingInit` for a workspace whose folder is away, and registry.ts:638 sets `pendingIdentity`, so the rename lives only in the registry. `availability` adopts a folder's identity whenever the entry still has `pendingInit` and the folder's id is not registered (registry.ts:718-727). The adoption runs `Object.assign(entry, entryFromIdentity(...))`, which overwrites `name` and `color` with the folder's values (registry.ts:724), and it clears only `pendingInit`. `pendingIdentity` stays set, so the user's offline rename is gone and nothing tells them: no toast, no `different` state. Before this change, edit deleted `pendingInit` unconditionally, so this adoption could not run after an offline edit; the folder showed as `different` and the rename survived.

Failure: rename a pendingInit workspace while its drive is away, then bring back a folder at that path whose identity.json carries an id this Mac does not know. The next probe (listState, or any availability call) renames the entry to the folder's name.

Fix for this path: refuse that adoption while the entry carries the user's pending edit, by adding `&& !entry.pendingIdentity` to the condition at line 718. The entry then reports `different` and keeps the edit, as it did before this change. The comment at 719 gives the adoption's reason (an identity that arrived while unreachable wins), and it does not mention edits, so this is the only path I am changing."},{"path":"apps/kaipu-record/src/renderer/src/features/workspaces/workspaces-context.tsx","line":168,"severity":"consider","topic":"tests","confidence":"high","title":"The toast suppression for an unchanged pick has no test","body":"The early return at line 168 is the only renderer change in this pull request, and no test reaches it. Grepping the app finds no test that asserts `folderChanged` or the `unchanged` skip. The only assertion is the flag itself (`relocate.test.ts:158`), and the dialog test mocks `onRelocated` (`workspace-dialog.test.tsx:50` and `:283`), so it never sees the context. A regression that shows the toast again, or one that hides the toast for a real move, would pass every current test. Add a provider-level test: an `ok` result with `unchanged: true` shows no toast, and a plain `ok` result still shows `folderChanged`."},{"path":"apps/kaipu-record/src/main/workspaces/registry.ts","line":189,"severity":"consider","topic":"cleanup","confidence":"high","title":"RelocateOutcome documents `unchanged`, but registry.relocate never sets it","body":"The `unchanged` field is declared on the registry's `RelocateOutcome` (registry.ts:188-189), which reads as a registry result. Only the wrapper sets it, at relocate.ts:44. `registry.relocate` (registry.ts:866-882) returns a plain `{ ok: true, entry }` even for the same path, and it still runs an `update` that writes preferences (registry.ts:870-876). A reader of the registry type would expect the flag from `relocate` and not get it. Move the field to the wrapper's return type in relocate.ts, or note in the comment that only `relocateWorkspace` sets it."}],"contracts":[{"action":"Pick the folder the workspace already points at in 'Change folder…' (same path)","location":"apps/kaipu-record/src/main/workspaces/relocate.ts:42-45","equivalent_path":"apps/kaipu-record/src/main/workspaces/switch-transaction.ts:96-133 (relocateActive, the active workspace); apps/kaipu-record/src/main/workspaces/registry.ts:866-882 (registry.relocate, other workspaces)","before_after":"Before: for the active workspace the pick ran prepareWindows, gate.close, the registry update that mirrors vaultDirectory, dropPendingCaptures, gate.commit (generation bump) and afterCommit. After: the function returns before all of those. The caller (index.ts:340-349) still runs the availability probe, refreshTitles and broadcastState. The same-path mirror write is skipped, which is safe because vaultDirectory already holds the active path: reconcile on open (registry.ts:351-353) and the mirror on every switch (registry.ts:958-962) keep them in step.","visible_effect":"No unsaved-changes question, no route remount, and no 'now points' toast (workspaces-context.tsx:167-168).","failure_mode":"The probe still runs after the early return, so a deleted identity.json is rewritten (registry.ts:733-742). No other failure is silent.","status":"closed","evidence":["apps/kaipu-record/src/main/workspaces/relocate.ts:42-45","apps/kaipu-record/src/main/workspaces/index.ts:340-349","apps/kaipu-record/src/main/workspaces/switch-transaction.ts:117-132","apps/kaipu-record/src/main/workspaces/registry.ts:351-353","apps/kaipu-record/src/main/workspaces/registry.ts:958-962","apps/kaipu-record/src/renderer/src/features/workspaces/workspaces-context.tsx:167-168"],"open_question":"","candidates":[]},{"action":"Rename or recolor a workspace whose folder is away and was never initialized (pendingInit), then 'Change folder…' to a folder with Kaipu items and no identity","location":"apps/kaipu-record/src/main/workspaces/registry.ts:632-638","equivalent_path":"apps/kaipu-record/src/main/workspaces/registry.ts:638 (the offline branch for an initialized workspace, which sets pendingIdentity only)","before_after":"Before: an offline edit deleted pendingInit, so a later relocate to such a folder was refused as has-items-no-identity. After: pendingInit stays until the folder is written, and the rename stays in the registry through pendingIdentity.","visible_effect":"Change folder accepts the moved folder (registry-relocate.test.ts:221-243). The dialog's save shows the editSavedOffline toast (workspaces-context.tsx:155-161).","failure_mode":"When the folder returns with another, unregistered identity, availability adopts that identity and overwrites the offline rename without any message (registry.ts:718-727). See the finding on registry.ts:718.","status":"closed","evidence":["apps/kaipu-record/src/main/workspaces/registry.ts:632-638","apps/kaipu-record/src/main/workspaces/registry.ts:718-727","apps/kaipu-record/src/main/workspaces/registry.ts:855","apps/kaipu-record/src/main/workspaces/registry-relocate.test.ts:221-243","apps/kaipu-record/src/renderer/src/features/workspaces/workspaces-context.tsx:155-161"],"open_question":"","candidates":[]},{"action":"workspaces:relocate result carries 'unchanged' for a same-folder pick, and the renderer skips the toast","location":"apps/kaipu-record/src/main/workspaces/index.ts:349","equivalent_path":"apps/kaipu-record/src/renderer/src/features/workspaces/workspaces-context.tsx:165-172 (onRelocated, the toast path that a real move already takes)","before_after":"Before: a same-path pick returned ok and showed folderChanged. After: it returns ok with unchanged: true and shows nothing. The dialog calls onRelocated directly (workspace-dialog.tsx:144-145), and Settings goes through changeFolder (workspaces-context.tsx:174-191), so both paths hit the same early return.","visible_effect":"Picking the current folder gives no feedback. That is the intended result, per the comment at workspaces-context.tsx:167.","failure_mode":"If the IPC call rejects, changeFolder shows relocateUncertain (workspaces-context.tsx:176-183). The flag is a plain field, so it cannot be lost on the way to the renderer.","status":"closed","evidence":["apps/kaipu-record/src/main/workspaces/index.ts:340-349","apps/kaipu-record/src/renderer/src/features/workspaces/workspaces-context.tsx:165-192","apps/kaipu-record/src/renderer/src/features/workspaces/workspace-dialog.tsx:144-145","apps/kaipu-record/src/shared/types/workspaces.ts:163-169"],"open_question":"","candidates":[]}],"thread_replies":[{"comment_id":4438597058,"status":"addressed","reply":"Addressed. registry.ts:643-647 now handles both rollback cases: it restores the old file when there was one, and removes the new file when there was none."},{"comment_id":4438597062,"status":"addressed","reply":"Addressed. index.ts:273-274 checks name and color separately and returns invalid-name or invalid-color."},{"comment_id":4438597064,"status":"addressed","reply":"Addressed. registry.ts:625-626 re-runs the name check inside the locked update and throws NameTakenError."},{"comment_id":4439290166,"status":"still_open","reply":"Partly addressed. The no-identity case is in place (registry.ts:855). The case where the moved folder already holds another id (registry.ts:843-845) is still open, as you noted in your reply. Separately, a new finding on the adoption path in availability (registry.ts:718) is posted in this review."},{"comment_id":4439290177,"status":"addressed","reply":"Addressed. relocate.ts:39-45 returns the unchanged entry before the transaction, so no window is asked to save and the generation stays put."},{"comment_id":4439336705,"status":"addressed","reply":"Addressed. relocate.ts:43-45 sets unchanged, index.ts:349 carries it over IPC, and workspaces-context.tsx:167-168 skips the toast. relocate.test.ts:158 asserts the flag."}],"summary":"Reviewed the seven files of this part. The changes do what the PR says: the same-folder pick returns early with a flag, the renderer skips the toast for it, and an offline edit keeps pendingInit so a later move is accepted. One fix-level bug: after an offline rename of a never-initialized workspace, availability adopts a returning folder's other identity and silently overwrites the rename (registry.ts:718). Two consider-level points: the renderer toast skip has no test, and the `unchanged` flag is documented on the registry type though only the wrapper sets it. Thread replies: the earlier rollback, color-validation and name-uniqueness threads are addressed; the registry.ts:809 thread is still open for the other-id case, as the owner noted. Nothing was built or run; all checks are from reading the code."}

